New target which trying to determine(by passive fingerprinting) 
remote OS by set of parameters from initial SYN packet which was sent to
us.

Fingerprints must be loaded through procfs (/proc/sys/net/ipv4/OSF).
For information about fingerprints please see help for OSF matching
module.

  Example:
  # iptables -I INPUT -j OSF -p tcp

Run and see syslog. You will find something like this:

  ipt_OSF: Windows [Windows XP Pro SP1, 2000 SP3]: 11.22.33.55:4024 ->
11.22.33.44:139

NOTE: -p tcp is obviously required as it is a TCP match.


All OSF patches(help, config...) actually are osf.patch set with a bit
changed content, so please review them, since i nderstand not very well
how patch-o-matic works :).

OSF was tested with 2.6-test9 (with uncommented line number 66) and it
works stable.
I've only compiled OSF target module with 2.4, without any testing.

Please test and apply.
Thank you.

	Evgeniy Polyakov ( s0mbre )

